WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.880
The SCP Foundation has gone up against a lot
of anomalies that can best be described as…

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.080
demonic.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:14.460
But few fit the bill better than the demons
and imps of SCP-5049, Demon Dan’s Discount

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:21.300
Homonculus Depot, a skin-stealing enterprise
designing bespoke demonic disguises on the

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.060
behalf of Seven Mysterious Demon Lords.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.640
Anyone that the Foundation has managed to&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.640
capture related to this&nbsp;
anomaly has been assassinated

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.920
by the Demon Lords, eliminating the prospect
of further investigation.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.420
But what if the Foundation brought in another
expert to help?

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.060
A bonafide expert in the occult.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:47.220
DC’s devious demon detective himself, John
Constantine.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:53.460
Maybe he can finally give us the lead we need
to bring down those Demon Lords once and for

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:53.640
all.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.280
And with the help of the Anom-O-Tron 6000,
we’re going to find out exactly how that

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.960
situation would play out.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.660
Let’s rev up the machine and take a look!

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.180
It was a cold night in New York; if you’ve
ever been there, you’ll know that most nights

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:09.600
are.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.900
But, on this particular night, a certain chill
was streaking its way through the air, as

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.640
icy cold as the grave.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.440
This wasn’t just a deathly gust of wind
or any other freak occurrence of the weather

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:28.440
though, especially judging by that piercing,
wailing shriek it gave as it passed by, a

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.560
cry loud enough to wake both the living and
the dead alike.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.040
And hot on its tail, chasing&nbsp;
through the rain-dampened&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.560
streets after it, long trench coat whipping

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.240
behind him, was the one man stupid enough
to try and catch it.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:48.780
You see, this thing he was chasing was a spirit;
some might have called it a Banshee or a Yonaki

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:54.000
babā, but all our coat-clad friend called
it was a ‘right bloody nuisance’.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.480
As for who in Heaven, in Hell or on Earth
he was?

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.560
That’s easy.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.600
If you were to rummage through the pockets
of his coat, you’d find the answer, along

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.600
with an interesting assortment of mystical
objects.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.640
Beneath the charms and trinkets that he carried
on his person was a crumpled off-white business

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.120
card.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:18.240
Printed on its surface, in simple black lettering
was one name: John Constantine.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.000
And underneath, along with a phone number,
were the words ‘Exorcist, Demonologist and

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.680
Master of the Dark Arts’ – although the
word ‘master’ had been crossed out, with

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.600
‘Petty Dabbler’ written above.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:34.140
Our friend John really hated putting on airs.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:39.780
He turned down an alleyway, just as the spirit
did, its screams rippling through the silence.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.440
Dead end, there was nothing but a solid wall
ahead.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:49.020
Not that it mattered, the shrieking entity
lacked a physical, corporeal form, but the

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:54.240
sight of an obstacle in its path caused it
to pause, just for a split second, a short

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.960
moment, as it tried to think: over or through?

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.900
And that tiny little instance of hesitation…

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.420
well, that’s what John had been waiting
for.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.980
As he ran towards the spirit, he reached into
his coat pocket, pulling out a lighter.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.349
Its surface was engraved with a phrase in
Latin, that read: ‘Fiat iustitia, et pereat

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:19.740
mundus’, meaning ‘Let justice be done,
though the world may perish’.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:25.200
That had long been John’s credo, to stop
at nothing to achieve righteous justice, no

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.720
matter what the cost or how bad things got.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:32.820
Admittedly, that was a little easier to accomplish
when you owned a blessed lighter.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.980
Striking it, John breathlessly uttered an
incantation to command the holy fire within.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:43.560
His hand caught ablaze as he took hold of
the flame, barely feeling the pain of it burning.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:49.380
Casting it towards the screeching spirit,
a bright orange streak shot forward and ensnared

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.400
the runaway creature.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.260
It hovered above the ground, writhing and
thrashing in the air as it struggled to free

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.300
itself from its fiery bonds.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.400
Shaking his hand to extinguish it, John reached
into his other pocket, looking for the small

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.660
jar he’d put there.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.360
To his horror, the glass container was gone.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.640
Constantine frantically patted the outside
of his coat, trying but unable to find it.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.320
He must have dropped it during their chase,
and without the jar, he had nothing to trap

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:16.980
the spirit in.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:21.900
“Typical,” he grumbled to himself, turning
to look at the shrieking specter wriggling

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.280
its way out of the flame.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.720
John looked around for something, anything
he could use to contain it.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:33.120
Finally, he spotted something left discarded
in the alleyway; it was an empty whiskey bottle,

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.160
filthy and covered in grime.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.560
“Well, s’pose this’ll have to do!”

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.840
Constantine said aloud to no one other than
himself; he was a bit of a fan of his own

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:48.240
voice, even if his overconfidence did regularly
cross the line into arrogance.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.160
Placing the bottle neck-up on a dry patch
of the ground, John hurriedly pulled a piece

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.360
of chalk from his pocket.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:59.640
He started to mark the asphalt, creating a
circle around the bottle, symbols taken from

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:04.200
ancient languages and magical texts surrounding
the unlikely vessel.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.240
His hands at his sides, Constantine took a
deep breath and began muttering in Aramaic;

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:14.160
to the untrained ear, it would have sounded
like an incomprehensible incantation, although

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.200
in no uncertain terms, John was just telling
the spirit to ‘pack it in and get in the

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.300
bottle before you wake the whole city’.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:26.880
With a final screech of dissatisfaction, the
entity was pulled into its cramped new home,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.080
like a mystical vacuum cleaner sucking up
a cloud of dust.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.740
With an exhausted sigh, John knelt down to
pick up the bottle.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:39.840
The glass surface was warm to the touch now
that the shrieking spirit was contained inside.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:45.000
He yawned, putting the bottle in the pocket
of his trench coat; he had a nice cosy shelf

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.680
back in the House of Mystery where he could
keep this troublesome siren and let it gather

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.340
dust, trapped and unable to cause harm to
any mortal ever again.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:55.860
But it was just as John was preparing a spell&nbsp;

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.440
to transport himself back&nbsp;
to his base of operations

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:00.900
that his cell phone started to ring.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.800
“Hello?” he answered bluntly; he was too
tired for whatever this was.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:06.180
“Um, hi.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.920
Is that Mr Constantine?”

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.560
a female voice asked from the other end of
the line.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.680
“Depends on who wants to know, love,”
John replied.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.820
“My name’s Emma.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:19.860
A friend of mine gave me your card, they said
that…” she paused, sounded like she was

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:20.520
sniffling.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.680
“They said you could help me get my brother
back.”

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:27.960
As much as it had already been a long night,
and even though he might often act like he

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:32.400
didn’t care, John was rarely heartless enough
to turn down a request for his help.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.080
Giving another sigh, John told Emma he’d
look into it, but she’d need to give him

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.460
the full story in person.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:44.280
The coffee shop was one of the few open this
early, as morning started to dawn over the

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:44.460
city.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:49.440
All of New York was gearing up for another
day of hustle and bustle, people shoving past

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.620
each other to get the subway to jobs they
hated.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:58.560
Stepping inside with his usual air of swagger
and bravado, John spotted Emma sitting and

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.280
waiting for him.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.260
She had a mug of coffee in her hands, but
wasn’t drinking it; the lack of steam seemed

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.180
to indicate it was already stone cold.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:11.520
“You must be Emma,” he greeted her, doing
his best impression of a friendly smile, extending

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:12.060
a handshake.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.400
“John Constantine, at your service.”

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.300
“Oh, hello,” Emma responded, awkwardly
accepting the shake.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.400
“You sure I can’t get you anything stronger?”

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.620
John offered as he sat down opposite.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.460
“Stronger?

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.280
It’s eight o’clock in the morning, isn’t
it a bit early for that?”

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.300
she asked.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.860
“Never too early in my book,” John chuckled
dryly, picking up a menu and scanning his

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:32.580
eyes over it.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.780
“Here we are, breakfast!

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:36.600
One should never battle demons on an empty
stomach.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.240
So, what can I do for you, Emma?” he asked,&nbsp;

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.240
not even looking up from&nbsp;
the menu, still half-focused

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:43.740
on what he was going to order.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:45.720
“Well,” Emma began.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:48.840
“Like I said over the phone, something happened
to my brother.”

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:50.580
“Run off, did he?”

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.720
Constantine interjected.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.440
“Yes.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.520
And no.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.560
Not exactly,” she sounded confused, like
she was aware that what she was attempting

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.800
to describe wouldn’t make any sense when
said out loud.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.920
“He did disappear, for a few days actually.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:10.020
We’ve been living together since our parents
died, in this tiny little apartment, so we

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.520
can tell when one of us has left.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:14.820
It was like, one moment he was there, the
next he wasn’t.”

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.960
“Sounds like a pretty run-of-the-mill missing
persons case, love,” John sighed.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.520
“Not exactly my department.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.580
You’re best off going to the coppers for
something like that.”

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.660
“I tried that!”

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:28.860
Emma raised her voice slightly, getting agitated…
or scared.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.680
“I told the cops Ethan was missing, and
they filed a report.

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.300
But they dropped the case when he…”

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:38.280
John thought about making another snide comment
to get her to finish her sentence, but chose

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.300
to wait instead.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.240
“He came home, just like that, a few days
later.

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.200
The police questioned Ethan and asked him
where he’d been, and he just told them he

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.320
had gone to a hotel for a few nights,” she
explained.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:51.360
“Open and shut, then,” John shrugged.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:56.700
“Except… the thing that came back, it’s
not my brother,” Emma continued, trying

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.140
to hold back frightened tears.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:02.340
“It looks like him, and it even sounds like
him, but… it’s not Ethan.”

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.260
“You think something happened to him?”

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:05.880
Constantine pondered.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:06.360
“Maybe.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.280
I don’t know about… possessions and demons
and all that stuff, but I was told you might

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:12.120
be able to help.”

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:16.500
“As much as I’d love to help you out,
I’m afraid I need a little more to go on

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:20.700
than that,” John admitted, a tiny shred
of sympathy in his tired eyes.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.840
“I recorded this!”

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.760
Emma exclaimed, producing her phone.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.900
“That’s part of what made me call you,
since he came back Ethan…

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.320
well, not Ethan, he started staying up late
at night.”

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.940
“Doing what, exactly?”

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.040
the paranormal detective asked.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.340
“Chanting,” she answered, hitting play
on her phone.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:43.860
The audio recording started, it was faint,
but John could just about hear someone growling.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:48.480
It was a human voice, male as expected, but
it sounded all wrong.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:54.300
Ethan, or whatever was pretending to be him,
was making noises closer to that of a wild

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.580
animal than a person, speaking in a garbled,
unintelligible tongue that sounded distinctly…

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.360
demonic, to John’s experienced ears.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:05.820
“What was he doing the night&nbsp;
before he disappeared?”&nbsp;

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:08.220
he asked after a solemn moment’s pause.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.200
“Just sitting at home, watching TV, nothing
out of the ordinary,” Emma answered.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.100
“But specifically,” John said with urgency
in his voice.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.960
“What was he watching?”

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:21.180
“I…
I don’t know!”

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:22.020
she exclaimed.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:25.800
“He was just flicking through channels,
but there was hardly anything on that late

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.180
except… ads.”

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:30.360
Leaning back in his seat, John tutted to himself,
shaking his head.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.900
“Demon Dan, you old codger,” he muttered.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.220
“Who’s Demon Dan?”

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.300
Emma asked.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.360
“I’m so sorry, love,” John replied,
dodging the question.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.800
“But your brother’s gone.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.240
And right now, there’s some nasty blighter
from the pits of Hell itself using his skin

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.400
as its own personal human disguise.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.040
We need to find it, and send ‘em all the
way down South.”

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:50.940
“South?”

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.100
Emma echoed, too confused to cry.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.080
“You mean like… to New Jersey?”

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.760
John smirked dryly.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.700
“Oh, much further than that, love,” he
chuckled.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.520
“Now, where would Ethan usually be at this
early hour?”

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:05.820
“Normally, he isn’t up this early, he’ll
be asleep back at the apartment.”

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.780
“Perfect!”

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.660
Constantine clapped his hands and stood up
from the table.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.580
“Ever seen an exorcism before?”

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.260
Hurriedly, Emma escorted John back to the
apartment she and her brother had shared.

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:21.780
There, they found Ethan – or rather, the
thing pretending to be him – seemingly laying

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:22.560
sound asleep.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:27.540
It was only as John approached, hands raised
cautiously, that the disguised demon rose

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.020
and lunged at him, snarling like a rabid animal
again.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:36.300
Luckily, while the entity within was a powerful
agent of darkness, the outer shell it was

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.160
wearing was still mostly human.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.920
A quick blow from a frying pan connected with
‘Ethan’s head, thanks to Emma, and knocked

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.320
him out long enough for John to make preparations.

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:51.300
Clearing the floor, ripping up the carpet
to gain access to the floorboards below, John

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.720
and Emma shifted the unconscious Ethan into
the center of the room.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:59.040
Around him, Constantine began marking out
a ritual circle on the woodwork.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:04.440
He’d brought along his bag, producing a
series of candles from it, placing each one

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:07.320
at the points of a pentagram he drew within
the circle.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:13.560
Buried in the bag were a few extra tools of
his many trades, some extra spell books, holy

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:16.200
water, and even some hallowed brass knuckles.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:21.000
He pulled one of the knuckledusters out and
pocketed it; he hadn’t used them in a dog’s

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.860
age, but better to be safe.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:27.720
“You didn’t answer before,” Emma chimed
in, watching the demonologist at work.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.500
“Come again?”

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.980
John replied as he started painting runes
around the pentagram.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.400
“When I asked you who Demon Dan was,”
she clarified.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.360
“A right pain in the backside, I’ll tell
you that for nothing,” he chuckled.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:42.720
“Think of him like the used car salesman
of the Underworld.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.320
I’ve only ever heard stories mind you, I
wasn’t certain until you mentioned that

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.000
Ethan was watching ads on the telly.”

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.080
“So, what?”

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.160
Emma asked.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.740
“This Demon Dan guy, he has his own commercials?”

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.640
“Spot on!”

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:54.960
John smirked.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.380
“He runs some place called Demon Dan’s
Discount Homunculus Depot.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:03.480
The ad appears on your TV, usually at random,
and then Dan starts hawking in wares.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:06.000
You know, real salesman type, that whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:06.900
infomercial
lark.”

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:08.400
“What’s he selling, though?”

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.900
she cut in, her voice telling John she had
already half figured it out, but didn’t

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:16.440
want the answer to be as horrible as the one
in her head.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:21.780
John paused for a moment, looking up from
the nearly-complete circle of occult symbols.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.940
“Us,” he replied plainly.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.080
“Human beings.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:30.540
Once the ad’s over, the nearest door becomes
a gateway to his little corner of paradise.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:32.400
Whoever sees it ends up there.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:37.200
That’s when Dan hollows a person out, scoops
out their soul until they’re just a husk.

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.120
That’s what happened to poor Ethan here.”

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:41.280
Emma sniffled, holding back tears.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.120
“But why?”

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.480
“Demons need vessels, love,” Constantine
answered.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:48.360
“They can’t well be running about up here
in broad daylight.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:52.020
That’s what Dan does, he takes them apart
and stitches them back up.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:56.580
Turns human beings into bespoke skin vehicles
for the worst Hell has to offer.”

00:13:56.580 --> 00:14:00.960
With the circle finally complete, John retrieved
one of his spell books and a vial of holy

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:01.920
water from his bag.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.060
It was time.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:08.460
Opening the book to the right chapter, he
splashed some of the blessed liquid over ‘Ethan’

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.780
laying in the middle of the circle.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:15.180
Instantly he woke up again, growling angrily
as the water singed his skin like burning

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:15.720
acid.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:19.920
Even through its disguise, it was still enough
to sting the demon.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:25.260
It went to lunge at the English exorcist again,
only to find an invisible barrier blocking

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:31.200
its path – the spell John had cast was working,
keeping the monster contained… for now.

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:36.540
“You…” the demon gurgled from inside
its skin suit, lifting a finger to John.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.660
“You are known to us, Constantine!”

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.480
“Oh yeah?” he replied sarcastically.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.300
“My reputation has a habit of preceding
me.”

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:50.160
“Indeed,” the creature replied, chuckling
in a mocking fashion.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.440
“We know what you’ve done.

00:14:52.440 --> 00:14:56.400
Your transgressions, your mistakes…

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:58.920
oh, so many failures.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:04.920
The great John Constantine, nothing but a
fraud.”

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:09.600
“That’s enough out of you, mate,” John
spat; flicking through the pages of his tome,

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.100
looking for the right incantation.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.440
“Your mother and father…”

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:15.000
the demon growled.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:20.160
“Mary Ann, Thomas… and Cheryl, your sister.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.080
Was it worth it, John?

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:28.200
A spell to make you a powerful magician, was
it really worth the fire that claimed their

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:28.860
lives?”

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:33.780
John forced himself to ignore the demon’s
taunting, beginning to mutter a spell under

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:34.380
his breath.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:39.480
All the while, he was aware that Emma was
standing next to him; he could see her concerned,

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.640
frightened look out of the corner of his eye.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:47.760
“And then poor, defenseless Astra,” the
hellspawn continued.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:54.240
“Practically handed over to Nergal on a
sliver platter, and all thanks to you, John.”

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.900
“I told you,” John smirked, finally reaching
the right passage.

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:58.980
“That’s enough!”

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:04.200
The whole room shook, books flying off shelves
as if the full force of an earthquake had

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:04.860
hit the apartment.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:09.900
In fact, it was worse than that, it was as
though a tornado was blasting through the

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:13.680
place, magical gusts of wind throwing everything
into disarray.

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:19.260
Images bombarded Constantine’s mind, the
sights that Ethan would have seen the night

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:20.340
he was taken.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:25.680
He could see the commercial on the TV, the
logo for Demon Dan's Discount Homunculus Depot

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.620
appearing on-screen in baby-blue bubble lettering.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:35.460
Then, there was the monster himself, Demon
Dan, his dark green skin, patches of thick

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:37.920
brown fur appearing randomly over his body.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:44.040
Next came the sight of the store itself, the
rows upon rows of hanging human corpses, all

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:48.000
hollowed-out shells ready for Dan’s demonic
customers to slip inside.

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.520
But all the while, John didn’t let up.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:55.440
Slinging more holy water at the disguised
demon, he shouted the words to the spell as

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:58.920
loud as he could, repeating the entire passage
over and over.

00:16:58.920 --> 00:17:03.900
Inside the circle, the creature thrashed and
growled, hovering above the ground as the

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.240
hellish host was forced out of Ethan’s remains.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:09.540
“The Seven Lords are ever planning their
invasion!”

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:11.220
the demon snarled.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:14.160
“You can’t stop what’s coming, Constantine!”

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.420
“If I had a quid for every time I heard
that,” John chuckled.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:23.940
With a final, deafening crash, the body finally
dropped back to the ground, still and lifeless.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:29.040
Emma couldn’t help but scream as she looked
at her brother, deflated, emptied inside,

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:32.340
and now left and little more than his empty
skin.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.780
“No, time for that, love!”

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:38.040
Constantine urged her, pulling his phone from
his pocket and typing out an urgent ‘SOS’

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:38.400
text.

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:39.840
“Now we’re in real trouble!”

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:41.520
“What the hell do you mean ‘real trouble’?”

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:45.540
Emma yelled, sobbing uncontrollably as she
cradled Ethan’s hollow body.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.800
“Well, Demon Dan’s not gonna be too pleased
when one of his customers complains about

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:54.960
what I just did,” John replied, checking
his phone; she hadn’t texted back yet, this

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:55.560
was an emergency.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:58.200
“So, he’ll probably be here any second
now-”

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:04.500
Practically on-cue, the front door to the
apartment swung open, and out stepped Demon

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:05.400
Dan himself.

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:10.860
He towered over both John and Emma, almost
seven feet tall on his long goat legs, and

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:12.900
even uglier than he had looked on TV.

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:19.500
“I should have known!” he bellowed, showing
off rows of pointed teeth as he laughed.

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:24.180
“If it isn’t the Hellblazer himself.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:28.620
You’ve got some nerve messing with my business,
little man!”

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:32.760
“And you’ve got some bloody cheek snatching
human beings for your little hustle, mate,”

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:37.260
John retorted, slipping something out of his
coat pocket as he squared up to the grotesque,

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.460
green-skinned demon.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:40.080
“A few words of advice, lad.

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:42.600
Cash up, pack your bags, and close shop.”

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.620
Demon Dan threw his head back and laughed,
a twisted, inhuman sound.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:52.980
“Or what?” he snarled with a grin.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:54.600
“I’ve got a thriving enterprise.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:57.360
Business is booming!

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.720
Do you really think you can stop me all alone,
Constantine?”

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:03.960
John smirked, feeling his phone buzz in his
pocket.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.340
“Who said I was alone?”

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:11.400
A blast of magical energy lit up the apartment,
as a raven-haired woman appeared, in a black

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:16.020
tuxedo jacket and matching top-hat, a white
shirt and bow-tie beneath.

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:19.860
She gave a flick of her hand, right towards
Dan, casting a spell.

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.327
“Dnes mih ot yrotagrup!”

00:19:21.327 --> 00:19:23.160
she yelled, all her words reversed.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:28.200
Before the demonic salesman could comprehend
what was going on, a portal erupted behind

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.360
him, with enough force to drag him into it.

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:35.460
Demon Dan tried desperately to scrabble to
grip at the floorboards, only to feel a shoe

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:36.960
standing on his clawed fingers.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.980
Looking down at him, John was wearing something
metal over his fingers.

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.900
“You’re out of business, mate.”

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:48.000
With a swing of his fist, the hallowed brass
knuckles smashed into Demon Dan’s face,

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:53.100
burning his green skin and sending him tumbling
backwards into the portal’s magical pull.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:56.280
“You took your time,” John jokingly scolded.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:00.360
“A ‘thank-you’ wouldn’t go a miss,
John,” Zatanna Zatara sighed.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.940
“I didn’t have to come just because you
texted me.”

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:05.880
“Cheers,” Constantine said earnestly.

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:10.980
He knew that Demon Dan wouldn’t be gone
for long, but maybe a short stint in Purgatory

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:13.620
would at least put a halt&nbsp;
to the satanic salesman’s&nbsp;

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.000
schemes for the time being.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:20.400
Although, swept up in the excitement of his
temporary victory, John didn’t notice Emma’s

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:23.820
eyes quickly flash an infernal shade of red.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:29.100
Now go check out “SCP-738 THE DEVIL’S
DEAL” to be made an offer you won’t be

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:30.000
able to refuse.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:34.920
Or, if you want more clashes between comic
book icons and creatures of chaos, then try

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.980
“DEADPOOL VS SCP-682” for more!

